  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo></math>Sum of the coefficients in the expansion of</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p>(putting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>)</p><p>Now, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo></math>Sum of the coefficients in the expansion of</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></math></p><p>Clearly, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>.</p>",
